Latest fix: bookmark placement drag and viewport-edge docking

- Repaired bookmark dragging without hiding, fading, moving, resizing, or restyling the actual Tab Peek overlay while a bookmark drag is in progress.
- Removed the added grip button from horizontal bookmark bars; drag the bar itself. Icon-only mode keeps the expand/collapse button centered and uses only the plain divider below it as the drag surface.
- Fixed Windowed-mode edge detection so top/bottom are detected against the browser viewport, not the floating panel's horizontal position.
- Top/bottom bookmark bars span the entire viewport width and sit flush against the browser edge.
- Windowed mode never reserves space by shifting or shrinking the overlay. Existing saved offsets from the previous behavior are cleared and reversed once.
- Only top/bottom placement on a vertical docked sidebar reserves 36px by shortening the sidebar; left/right placement remains adjacent to the overlay.
- The translucent preview shows the full-width bookmark bar; the panel destination preview is shown only when a docked vertical sidebar actually needs to shorten.
- Kept the existing expanded-bookmark hover-switch behavior.
- Included every current root extension file in the nested folder; content.js, defaults.js, README.md, tp-bookmarks.js, and tp-css.js are the modified copies. Backup remains excluded.
